#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# A PAINT SESSION HOST. The counterpart to chess_lobby.etcs, and the same shape
# for the same reason: a browser has no listening socket, so the page that is
# drawing cannot be the thing viewers connect to. This node is.
#
#     etcs modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_lobby.etcs
#     then point a paint page's share menu at http://<this host>:8081/art
#
# IT HOLDS NO DOCUMENT. Sessions, rosters, tokens and notebook entries as text
# -- see PaintNode's header note on why a relay that decoded its payload would
# need rebuilding every time the payload grew.
#
# AddRequestRoute, NOT AddRoute. This node reads the request METHOD (a push is a
# POST, a read is a GET) and the request BODY, and the older path-string route
# carries neither. It also answers by reference, which is what lets a read of a
# session return more than 255 bytes -- see HttpServer::DispatchRoute.

spawn PaintProvider::PaintNode art
art.Mount(art)

ensure NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8081)
web.AddRequestRoute(@art Request @art Filter)

# The paint page is served from wherever it is served from, which need not be
# here -- so a session's viewers are cross-origin by default and the node has to
# say so. Same line, same reason, as chess_web.etcs.
web.AddHeader(Access-Control-Allow-Origin *)

# A push is a POST, and a cross-origin POST is preflighted the moment it carries
# anything but a form content type. The page sends text/plain deliberately to
# stay a simple request; these two lines are what keep that true if it ever
# stops being.
web.AddHeader(Access-Control-Allow-Methods GET, POST, OPTIONS)
web.AddHeader(Access-Control-Allow-Headers Content-Type)

web.Start()
